        ⛔ THE SIZE COLUMN IS NOT THE TIME COLUMN IN ANY SENSE THAT MATTERS.
        Image size does cost something -- 0.0243 ms per MiB, at or just
        above this instrument's floor -- but carried across the whole
        196 MiB that separates our kdenlive bundle from the
        competitor's it is 4.8 ms of a gap that has never been
        observed smaller than 129 ms. The byte levers --cut,
        --fixpoint and the debloat rules cannot close it, so the struck
        size work stays struck and the cold cost is a FIXED price for
        standing the mount up. TODO/PROGRESS.md N6 is where it is paid.

